.html) to incorporate this logic.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Workflow**\n\nI'm now revising my approach by directly integrating the certificate generation process into `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html`. The updated plan involves `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html` functioning as the main app, beginning with a dashboard overlay. Upon filling out input fields (Student Name, Role, etc.) and clicking \"Generate,\" the overlay hides. Then, the certificate appears, and the PDF download is initiated automatically. I'm focusing on the user experience and have made the new `index.html` the dashboard.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI'm now completely restructuring. I'm abandoning query parameters for security, aiming for a single-page app structure. `index.html` will now act as the full application. It will contain both the dashboard and the certificate UI, hidden initially. Upon \"Generate\" click, I'll dynamically fetch, parse, and modify `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html`, append it invisibly, generate the PDF, and then remove it. I'll also add a `package.json` with `@vercel/kv` and create `api/get-number.js`. The dashboard UI will also be completed. Finally, the file `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html` will be renamed to a simpler name.\n\n\n**Updating Repository Structure**\n\nI've renamed `IIC_Certificate_Generator.html` to `template.html` and examined the user's GitHub repo, noting the existing files. Now, I'm focused on creating a `package.json` to include `@vercel/kv`, and then implementing the `/api/generate.js` route. This API route will handle certificate number generation and storage using Vercel KV, ensuring a maximum of 70 certificates are issued. I'll include input validation and appropriate error handling.\n\n\n**Refining UI Implementation**\n\nI'm now focusing on the user interface and have decided on a premium, dark-themed design for `index.html`, which will be the central dashboard. It will have a \"Generate Official Certificate\" button and include inputs for Full Name, and a Role selection. I'll dynamically inject values into `template.html`, which will be rendered in a hidden div, and use `html2canvas` and `jspdf` for PDF generation, upon the user clicking the generate button.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$code = @\\\"\\nimport os\\nimport json\\n\\nbase_dir = r'C:\\\\Users\\\\prsnl\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\d1b69639-1940-4d3a-9d7d-b4963cb4837c'\\n\\n# 1. Create package.json for Vercel KV\\npackage_json = {\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"iic-certificate-portal\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@vercel/kv\\\": \\\"^1.0.1\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\nwith open(os.path.join(base_dir, 'package.json'), 'w') as f:\\n    json.dump(package_json, f, indent=2)\\n\\n# 2. Create api directory and serverless function\\napi_dir = os.path.join(base_dir, 'api')\\nos.makedirs(api_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\napi_code = '''import { kv } from '@vercel/kv';\\n\\nexport default async function handler(req, res) {\\n  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\\n    return res.status(405).json({ error: 'Method not allowed' });\\n  }\\n  \\n  try {\\n    // Increment the global counter in Vercel KV\\n    const newCount = await kv.incr('iic_cert_counter');\\n    \\n    // Hard cap at 70 certificates\\n    if (newCount > 70) {\\n      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Registration closed. All 70 certificates have been claimed.' });\\n    }\\n    \\n    // Format to 3 digits (e.g., 001, 002)\\n    const formattedNumber = String(newCount).padStart(3, '0');\\n    const certId = `ACE/IIC/2025-26/${formattedNumber}`;\\n    \\n    return res.status(200).json({ certId, count: newCount });\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Database connection error. Please ensure Vercel KV is linked in the Vercel Dashboard.' });\\n  }\\n}\\n'''\\nwith open(os.path.join(api_dir, 'generate.js'), 'w') as f:\\n    f.write(api_code)\\n\\nprint('Vercel Backend setup complete.')\\n\\\"@\\nSet-Content -Path setup_backend.py -Value $code\\npython setup_backend.py\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\prsnl\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\d1b69639-1940-4d3a-9d7d-b4963cb4837c\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Creating the Vercel API backend and package.json to securely handle the Vercel KV global counter math\"","toolSummary":"\"Setup Vercel Backend\""}}]}
{"step_index":1657,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:41:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-29T21:11:57+05:30\nTool is running as a background task with task id: d1b69639-1940-4d3a-9d7d-b4963cb4837c/task-1657\nTask Description: $code = @\"\nimport os\nimport json\n\nbase_dir = r'C:\\Users\\prsnl\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\d1b69639-1940-4d3a-9d7d-b4963cb4837c'\n\n# 1. Create package.json for Vercel KV\npackage_json = {\n  \"name\": \"iic-certificate-portal\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@vercel/kv\": \"^1.0.1\"\n  }\n}\nwith open(os.path.join(base_dir, 'package.json'), 'w') as f:\n    json.dump(package_json, f, indent=2)\n\n# 2. Create api directory and serverless function\napi_dir = os.path.join(base_dir, 'api')\nos.makedirs(api_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\napi_code = '''import { kv } from '@vercel/kv';\n\nexport default async function handler(req, res) {\n  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\n    return res.status(405).json({ error: 'Method not allowed' });\n  }\n  \n  try {\n    // Increment the global counter in Vercel KV\n    const newCount = await kv.incr('iic_cert_counter');\n    \n    // Hard cap at 70 certificates\n    if (newCount > 70) {\n      return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Registration closed. All 70 certificates have been claimed.' });\n    }\n    \n    // Format to 3 digits (e.g., 001, 002)\n    const formattedNumber = String(newCount).padStart(3, '0');\n    const certId = `ACE/IIC/2025-26/${formattedNumber}`;\n    \n    return res.status(200).json({ certId, count: newCount });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Database connection error. Please ensure Vercel KV is linked in the Vercel Dashboard.' });\n  }\n}\n'''\nwith open(os.path.join(api_dir, 'generate.js'), 'w') as f:\n    f.write(api_code)\n\nprint('Vercel Backend setup complete.')\n\"@\nSet-Content -Path setup_backend.py -Value $code\npython setup_backend.py\nTask logs are available at: file:///C:/Users/prsnl/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d1b69639-1940-4d3a-9d7d-b4963cb4837c/.system_generated/tasks/task-1657.log"}
